# 301 redirects. Cloudflare Pages + Netlify both read this file.
# Format: /old-path/  /new-path/  301
# Add one line whenever a slug changes or an old WordPress URL needs to point to the new site.
# Carried over from the live site's _redirects, with targets updated to the new trailing-slash URLs.
# Every page keeps its URL, now with a trailing slash. Netlify and Cloudflare Pages redirect
# /about-us -> /about-us/ by themselves, so only the old .html forms need explicit rules.

# Old .html forms (the live site served these through the host's pretty-URL redirect)
/index.html /  301
/seo-services.html /seo-services/ 301
/website-development.html /website-development/ 301
/about-us.html /about-us/ 301
/contact.html /contact/ 301
